//? Title: D* Lite on a Changing Grid: Retained Labels, Actual Repairs and Moving Starts
//? Subtitle: The original two-by-two route, a blocked corridor, obstacle discoveries and measured reuse
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given a grid map, a start and a goal, we want an optimal route that can
be repaired when obstacles change or the start moves. Starting a new
search after every discovery discards useful earlier distance labels.
D* Lite keeps committed and one-step cost-to-go estimates and repairs
only the inconsistent frontier needed for the current query. We retain
the original two-by-two example, expose actual lower/raise/key-refresh
operations, and follow a map through a detour, a complete wall and a
reopened doorway. Measured work compares retained state with fresh
runs of the same kernel. The original one-shot function remains
available, while a new persistent canonical C++ planner provides the
incremental state the earlier D*-style example did not retain.
)

\toc

> Start with the original two-by-two grid

Use four-neighbor unit movement on an empty two-by-two occupancy grid.
Start at (row 0, column 0), and fix the goal at (1,1). An optimal route
has two edges and includes three cells. The original d_star_replan
entry point still returns that result. It now constructs a fresh D* Lite
planner; retaining a DStarLiteGrid object across calls is what enables
incremental reuse.

D* Lite searches backward from the goal. A committed label g(u) and
one-step label rhs(u) are initially infinite, except rhs(goal)=0.
The first actual pop lowers the goal's g to zero. Its two neighbors
receive rhs=1, and the start eventually receives g=rhs=2. The table
shows all four actual pops, and the native diagram shows the repaired
labels and the returned route. Coordinates are zero-based (row, column).

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dstar_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto grid=dm::algorithms::grid_obstacle_mask(2,2);
  dm::algorithms::DStarLiteGrid planner(grid,{0,0},{1,1});
  const auto t=planner.repair_trace();
  const auto text=[](std::uint64_t x){return x==dm::algorithms::d_star_infinity?std::string("inf"):std::to_string(x);};
  std::print("Original grid: found {}; cost {:.0f}; inclusive cells {}; trace entries {}.\n\n",t.repair.route.found,t.repair.route.cost,t.repair.route.path.size(),t.captured_entries);
  std::print("| popped cell | stored key | g before | rhs before | g after | rhs after |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n");
  for(const auto& s:t.steps)
    std::print("| ({},{}) | ({},{}) | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",s.vertex/2,s.vertex%2,s.old_key.first,s.old_key.second,text(s.g_before),text(s.rhs_before),text(s.g_after),text(s.rhs_after));
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(88,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=2.6;box.height=1.3;box.font_size=23;
  for(std::size_t u=0;u<4;++u) {
    box.fill=u==0?dm::graphics::RGB{187,247,208}:u==3?dm::graphics::RGB{254,215,170}:dm::graphics::RGB{239,246,255};
    d.node(std::to_string(u),{3.5*(u%2),-3.5*static_cast<double>(u/2)},std::format("({},{}){}\ng={}; rhs={}",u/2,u%2,u==0?" S":u==3?" G":"",t.final_g[u],t.final_rhs[u]),box);
  }
  dm::graphics::DiagramStroke route;route.color={37,99,235};route.width=3;
  for(std::size_t i=1;i<t.repair.route.path.size();++i) {
    const auto a=t.repair.route.path[i-1],b=t.repair.route.path[i];
    d.edge(std::to_string(2*a.first+a.second),std::to_string(2*b.first+b.second),"cost 1",route);
  }
  d.text({1.75,1.4},"Original route: two unit edges; backward goal labels",25)
   .save_svg("build/dstar_tiny.svg");
}
```
