> Follow one planner through discoveries, movement and a new doorway

Use a six-by-twelve free grid, start (2,1), goal (2,10). The initial
cost is nine. An unchanged query and an off-route edit at (5,0) keep
that cost. Blocking (2,6) forces an eleven-step detour. The caller then
moves the start to the next cell on that returned route; the remaining
cost is ten. Closing the entire column 6 removes every route.
Opening its cell (3,6) creates a doorway and restores a cost-twelve route.
The goal remains fixed throughout.

A moving start changes Manhattan priorities. For each relocation a→b,
update kₘ←kₘ+h(a,b). The triangle inequality gives
h(a,b)+h(b,u)≥h(a,u), so old stored keys remain lower bounds on
current keys. A popped old key that is too small is refreshed before
label expansion. This avoids eagerly rebuilding the entire queue on
movement. Modifier arithmetic reserves 4N headroom below the integer
infinity sentinel and rejects overflow before changing the start.

Each table row compares retained repair pops with a newly initialized
D* Lite run on the same current map/start/goal. Pending map/start-update
work belongs to that repair's counters. A zero pop count does not mean
the API did no work: edits still perform Bellman backups, and returning
a route still visits/copies its cells.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dstar_discoveries.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::algorithms::DStarLiteGrid p(dm::algorithms::grid_obstacle_mask(6,12),{2,1},{2,10});
  std::vector<dm::algorithms::DStarTrace> stage;
  stage.push_back(p.repair_trace());stage.push_back(p.repair_trace());
  p.update_cells({{{5,0},true}});stage.push_back(p.repair_trace());
  p.update_cells({{{2,6},true}});stage.push_back(p.repair_trace());
  p.move_start(stage.back().repair.route.path[1]);stage.push_back(p.repair_trace());
  std::vector<dm::algorithms::GridCellUpdate> wall;
  for(int row=0;row<6;++row)wall.push_back({{row,6},true});
  p.update_cells(wall);stage.push_back(p.repair_trace());
  p.update_cells({{{3,6},false}});stage.push_back(p.repair_trace());
  const std::array<const char*,7> names{"initial","unchanged","off-route edit","route obstacle","move one step","closed wall","opened doorway"};
  std::print("| stage | found | cost if found | changed cells | start moves | vertex updates | repair pops | fresh pops | lower / raise / refresh |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<stage.size();++i) {
    const auto& t=stage[i];dm::algorithms::DStarLiteGrid fresh(t.blocked,t.start,t.goal);
    const auto cold=fresh.repair();const auto& w=t.repair.work;
    if(cold.route.found!=t.repair.route.found || cold.route.cost!=t.repair.route.cost)throw std::runtime_error("fresh/repair mismatch");
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} / {} / {} |\n",names[i],t.repair.route.found,t.repair.route.found?std::format("{:.0f}",t.repair.route.cost):"—",w.changed_cells,w.start_moves,w.vertex_updates,w.pops,cold.work.pops,w.lowerings,w.raisings,w.key_refreshes);
  }
  auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2,2);
  for(std::size_t i:{0u,3u,5u,6u}) {
    const auto& t=stage[i];auto plot=dm::algorithms::plot_grid_route(t.blocked,t.repair.route,t.start,t.goal);
    plot.title(names[i]);layout.add(plot);
  }
  layout.size(1100,850).title("One persistent planner: route, detour, disconnection and restored doorway")
   .fit_panels().save_svg("build/dstar_discoveries.svg");
}
```
