\caption(One persistent planner retains its fields across seven updates/queries. Fresh same-kernel searches agree on every route cost and reachability result; counters include actual pending updates and lazy key refreshes.)
\alttext(Four grid panels show the original straight route, a detour around a blocked cell, an impassable column wall and a route through a reopened doorway, with row numbers increasing downward.)

The route obstacle takes 32 retained pops versus 30 fresh pops, and
the closed wall takes 38 versus 30. Reopening the doorway instead
takes 16 retained pops versus 34 fresh pops. The same planner can
therefore show both extra repair work and useful reuse.

> Measure reuse without promising every repair is cheaper

The indexed queue has at most N entries. Each insert/remove costs
O(log N); a Bellman backup checks at most four neighbors. Persistent
storage is O(N). A changed-cell batch costs O(k log N), with updates
applied in input order. A repair can still expand much of the map, so
reusing state is not a guarantee that each individual query beats a
fresh search. Zero-pop cases are useful evidence of reuse, rather than
a bound for every obstacle pattern.

The next controlled family uses three rows and C columns, start on the
middle row's left end and goal on its right end. A cold run solves the
straight corridor. An unchanged query, a one-cell move along that route
and an off-route corner obstacle reuse those labels. Finally a middle-
row obstacle forces a detour. A fresh planner on that final map supplies
the comparison. Requested widths are powers of two from 32 through 1024;
all measured route costs/reachability results are checked before plotting.
Queue-pop counts include refreshes as well as lower/raise expansions.
Allocation, validation, heap comparisons and route output are excluded
from these counters; neither panel measures CPU time or robot latency.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dstar_reuse.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> width,cold_pops,edit_pops,fresh_pops,ratio;
  std::print("| columns | cells | initial pops | unchanged pops | moved pops | off-route pops | route-edit pops | fresh final pops | final cost |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(int columns:{32,64,128,256,512,1024}) {
    dm::algorithms::DStarLiteGrid p(dm::algorithms::grid_obstacle_mask(3,columns),{1,0},{1,columns-1});
    const auto cold=p.repair();const auto unchanged=p.repair();
    p.move_start({1,1});const auto moved=p.repair();
    p.update_cells({{{0,0},true}});const auto off=p.repair();
    p.update_cells({{{1,columns/2},true}});const auto edited=p.repair();
    dm::algorithms::DStarLiteGrid fresh(p.grid(),p.start(),p.goal());const auto final=fresh.repair();
    if(!edited.route.found || edited.route.cost!=columns || final.route.cost!=edited.route.cost || unchanged.work.pops || moved.work.pops || off.work.pops)
      throw std::runtime_error("reuse-family invariant failed");
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.0f} |\n",columns,3*columns,cold.work.pops,unchanged.work.pops,moved.work.pops,off.work.pops,edited.work.pops,final.work.pops,edited.route.cost);
    width.push_back(std::log2(columns));cold_pops.push_back(cold.work.pops);edit_pops.push_back(edited.work.pops);fresh_pops.push_back(final.work.pops);ratio.push_back(1.0*edited.work.pops/final.work.pops);
  }
  auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  a.line(width,cold_pops,"initial",{22,163,74}).line(width,edit_pops,"repair",{37,99,235})
   .line(width,fresh_pops,"fresh final",{220,38,38})
   .title("Measured queue pops").x_label("log2(columns)").y_label("actual repair-loop pops")
   .y_limits(0,std::max({cold_pops.back(),edit_pops.back(),fresh_pops.back()})*1.3+1);
  auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  b.line(width,ratio,"edit / fresh",{37,99,235}).points(width,ratio,"",{37,99,235},5)
   .line(width,std::vector<double>(width.size(),0),"warm queries",{22,163,74})
   .title("This family: zero-pop reuse and a local edit").x_label("log2(columns)")
   .y_label("repair pops / fresh final pops").y_limits(-.05,*std::max_element(ratio.begin(),ratio.end())*1.35+.05);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,550)
   .title("Retained state versus fresh runs of the same unit-grid kernel")
   .fit_panels().save_svg("build/dstar_reuse.svg");
}
```
